---
import CastMock from './mocks/CastMock.astro'
---

  <section class="feat sc-cast" id="tv">
    <div class="wrap feat-in">
      <div class="feat-copy" data-reveal>
        <h2>Send it to the set, without repacking it first</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Cast to Chromecast, a DLNA TV or — from a Mac — an AirPlay TV from one button. Each TV in the list says what will happen to <i>this</i> file; when the set can play the release as it is — often 4K HEVC HDR with Dolby audio — nothing is re-encoded.
        </p>
        <ul class="checks">
          <li><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg>
            <span><b>Otherwise the file is remuxed</b>, with the video copied rather than re-encoded, so it is ready in seconds.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg>
            <span><b>A torrent can be cast while it downloads.</b></span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg>
            <span><b>The window becomes a remote:</b> keys, chapters and the queue control the TV, and disconnecting resumes on the computer.</span></li>
        </ul>
        <a class="more-link" href="/cast-to-tv">Casting, in detail</a>
      </div>
      <div class="feat-mock" data-reveal style="--dl:1">
        <CastMock />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
